# Exporter output. Every .3mf here is generated by map2model.py, so it is build
# output, not source -- and it churns on every run. The files stay on disk (and
# in OneDrive); they are just not tracked.
#
# One exception worth knowing: a .3mf that has been opened and saved in Bambu
# Studio carries slicer settings and plate layout that the exporter cannot
# reproduce. If you have tuned one, track it deliberately:
#     git add -f toyko.3mf
#
# Exports land in 3Dmodels/<name>/, one folder per model; *.3mf matches
# at any depth so the whole tree is covered.
*.3mf

# Python
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
.venv/
venv/

# Editor / OS
.vscode/
.idea/
Thumbs.db
desktop.ini
